{"summary":"Fix signed decimal padding in both stringification paths.","explanation":"The current tests show two related failures. In `CheckDec`, negative integers passed with zero padding (for example, `-1` at width 3) produce `0-1` instead of `-01`; with space padding, `-2104741142` at width 12 produces `- 2104741142` instead of ` -2104741142`. The test compares `expected` from `snprintf` with `actual` from `StrCat`. In `SubstituteTest.Substitute`, the `Dec(int16_t{-1}, kSpacePad5)` argument is expected to contribute `   -1`, but contributes `-   1`, yielding the reported full-string mismatch. Both `Dec` implementations calculate padding while including the sign, then place the fill on the wrong side of it. Calculate the padding width from the full signed representation and place zero fill after the sign, while placing space fill before it. This also preserves unpadded and already-wide values.","edits":[{"path":"absl/strings/str_cat.h","old":"    ptrdiff_t fillers = writer - minfill;
    if (fillers > 0) {
      // Tricky: if the fill character is ' ', then it's <fill><+/-><digits>
      // But...: if the fill character is '0', then it's <+/-><fill><digits>
      bool add_sign_again = false;
      if (dec.neg && dec.fill == ' ') {  // If filling with '0',
        ++writer;                    // ignore the sign we just added
        add_sign_again = true;       // and re-add the sign later.
      }
      writer -= fillers;
      std::fill_n(writer, fillers, dec.fill);
      if (add_sign_again) *--writer = '-';
    }","new":"    ptrdiff_t padding = writer - minfill;
    if (padding > 0) {
      if (dec.neg && dec.fill == '0') {
        ++writer;  // Place zero padding after the sign.
        writer -= padding;
        std::fill_n(writer, padding, dec.fill);
        *--writer = '-';
      } else {
        writer -= padding;
        std::fill_n(writer, padding, dec.fill);
      }
    }"},{"path":"absl/strings/substitute.cc","old":"  ptrdiff_t fillers = writer - minfill;
  if (fillers > 0) {
    // Tricky: if the fill character is ' ', then it's <fill><+/-><digits>
    // But...: if the fill character is '0', then it's <+/-><fill><digits>
    bool add_sign_again = false;
    if (neg && dec.fill == ' ') {  // If filling with '0',
      ++writer;                    // ignore the sign we just added
      add_sign_again = true;       // and re-add the sign later.
    }
    writer -= fillers;
    std::fill_n(writer, fillers, dec.fill);
    if (add_sign_again) *--writer = '-';
  }","new":"  ptrdiff_t padding = writer - minfill;
  if (padding > 0) {
    if (neg && dec.fill == '0') {
      ++writer;  // Place zero padding after the sign.
      writer -= padding;
      std::fill_n(writer, padding, dec.fill);
      *--writer = '-';
    } else {
      writer -= padding;
      std::fill_n(writer, padding, dec.fill);
    }
  }"}]}
